  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "At Oklahoma State University, iQ Foods founder Brandon Lobaugh used research facilities to develop his storage concept. Consulting for the National Cattlemen’s Beef Association had connected him with meat scientists and the university’s Food and Agricultural Products Center. Those professional relationships provided access to equipment and specialist expertise.\n\nHe also addressed the daily work of monitoring stored inventory. His company replaced repeated manual temperature rounds with wireless data loggers supplied through CAS Dataloggers. The system recorded readings from multiple locations and uploaded them automatically, allowing staff to check conditions remotely and produce records for customers and quality inspectors.",
    "html": "<p>At Oklahoma State University, iQ Foods founder Brandon Lobaugh used research facilities to develop his storage concept. Consulting for the National Cattlemen’s Beef Association had connected him with meat scientists and the university’s Food and Agricultural Products Center. Those professional relationships provided access to equipment and specialist expertise.</p>\r\n<p>He also addressed the daily work of monitoring stored inventory. His company replaced repeated manual temperature rounds with wireless data loggers supplied through CAS Dataloggers. The system recorded readings from multiple locations and uploaded them automatically, allowing staff to check conditions remotely and produce records for customers and quality inspectors.</p>\r\n",
    "word_count": 98,
